{title: My Rock}
{subtitle: Psalms 18:2–3}
{key: Em}
{tempo: 120}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Em] |
| [Em] | [Em] | [C] | [C] | ×3

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]I love you LORD my strength
[C]You are my rock and fortress
[Em]My God my crag of refuge
[C]My shield and my salva[Em]tion
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The LORD is [D]my rock my [C]fortress
My de[Em]liver[D]er my [C]stronghold
The [Em]horn [D]of my sal[C]vation
[Am7]My God [Bm]my safe [Em]place
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I call on the LORD worthy of praise
[C]And I am saved from my enemies
[Em]You hold me when the world shakes
[C]You keep me from falling
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Em]The LORD is [D]my rock my [C]fortress
My de[Em]liver[D]er my strong[C]hold
The [Em]horn of [D]my salva[C]tion
[Am7]My God [B]my safe [Em]place
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[C]I find my [D]rest in your shad[Em]ow
[C]Your strength is [D]my daily [Em]bread
[C]I sing to the [D]one who res[Em]cues me
From the [Am]grasp [B]of all my [Em]foes
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
You are [D]my rock for[C]ever
My [Em]strength [D]and my [C]song
{end_of_verse}

